\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}},\\,0<x<1\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281302 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "82618995-8e73-5f87-bf17-79a78614a421" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281302 #edb/ref 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/d6/d60700d57ddc72bb410b3136f546705676f83d23d9071ffe972c5163d11af549.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/75/75e0132cd3854f18e9ab409b7fd13af3898f78b5174647bf2b33b8438b9228cb.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<x<1\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281311 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186280885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281311 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161731" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281311 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281311 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/8d/8d7ceac8c936a745ae79f71844a6d1a74175b1b97a2a497588d34c9ff988cdf9.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<3,\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281311 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "808c27a2-2e52-5219-b992-2d2dd6f143c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281311 #edb/ref 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c0/c0e6ef400b15c54264a400af99bef64c3bb5aeb7ceadbdd599375c0f1e0d3642.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/8c/8c5bbdfca6736194791f834ab4aadb03a30e3f116e89ffd5a7ea3e0104708ae4.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<3,\\,0<y<\\frac{2}{3}x\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336091 #edb/ref 1080 "0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336091 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336091 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "07a430fa-18ac-5b72-b213-7419118f4d28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336389 #edb/ref 1080 "0\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336389 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336389 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "261681af-6b12-54ce-90d1-a8bbf77d214c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336596 #edb/ref 1080 "0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336596 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336596 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3bf8ee8f-a53d-5a4a-970b-d8f88bbf5f34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337661 #edb/ref 1080 "0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337661 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337661 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b7fe65d2-d5b1-57e7-967d-53f4f7eb8d9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338092 #edb/ref 1080 "0\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338092 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338092 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ec60a4d0-fed3-50cf-8700-ae050890c608" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338390 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338390 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338390 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338390 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338390 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186338092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338390 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338390 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338390 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186336596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338390 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3f1f5949-3ba9-562b-a461-7c260db2239f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339008 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339008 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71888" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339008 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339008 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0\\le y<2\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}},\\,0<y<2\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339008 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a329f0e7-fa8c-5ef6-8758-63f7881531f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339008 #edb/ref 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/f4/f4ee8fbf9a7670a7d0e0b7488bccbf014f8db8fff0154c7db025f2b071aec566.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/9f/9fc733f6966b016c93b6ee6a305c5af5ee4fa432dad5d95e28061fd2a0d33efb.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<y<2\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378850 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186378851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378850 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161623" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378850 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378850 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\nII. $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\nIII. $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378850 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7cfd8147-c3e0-5cab-9b14-cee4034ac307" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378850 #edb/ref 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c2/c2b4e3d11f16920ce24a279289808d3f5dc4e68563525f1417c8767a5446b461.png)\n\n \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378851 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378851 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378851 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378851 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378851 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378851 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378851 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378851 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186378852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378851 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5fce85d8-31bd-5894-a084-f12d40765a2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378852 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378852 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378852 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bd3c14e6-cdac-5b50-83d2-c7a7e936d3c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378853 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378853 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378853 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7e056cb0-ca61-54f2-a5e9-73842a82ebde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378854 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378854 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378854 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c9cb356d-0a4a-57bd-9dbf-4365785bf3de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378855 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378855 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378855 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d6fe1489-c5d9-51b7-a695-df2f0bfed8ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378856 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378856 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378856 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "301c3c2d-1689-5485-a99c-8b0d727eadbf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378871 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186378872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378871 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161649" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378871 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378871 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x\\ge {y}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A$\n\nII. $A⊂\\text{int}A$\n\nIII. $A-\\text{int}A=∂A$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378871 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6e963f0b-a2c7-5ae0-844a-f3e405d79aa4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378871 #edb/ref 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88f35519cf1aa01bcc9e4fb91b24c2bc2a1a823867ec2670563b0b45f2643a0a.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/64/649c33f1738a35f3d298038bd2cf05d3b435424a4efbbb1e6143cf0d56b2bfd6.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A.$\n\n- Statement II is false. In this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points, so we must have $A⊈\\text{int}A.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A-\\text{int}A=∂A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378872 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378872 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378872 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378872 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378872 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378872 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378872 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378872 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186378874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378872 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6419e7cc-8024-5bbd-a920-bed8d2a11d14" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378873 #edb/ref 1080 "None of the statements are true" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378873 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378873 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3224235d-c85f-581e-b0a5-fa619bf3e2c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378874 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378874 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378874 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0ec09210-3416-5440-a20c-8e780f2effa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378875 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378875 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378875 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2180dbea-78a1-57c5-87db-f486a6914b9a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378876 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378876 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378876 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3257f157-5b66-55fe-830a-873790844a65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378877 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378877 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378877 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7789b753-b1d3-5748-ae54-82d9e789e198" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398548 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398548 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161596" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398548 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398548 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/2b/2bb25857047d7a0200d4c58ee3756b0efa0f2d13aaca8664b1fe49414c18a461.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398548 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "28ca8dae-bb66-5179-8a04-f47a13f5a86d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398548 #edb/ref 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88f35519cf1aa01bcc9e4fb91b24c2bc2a1a823867ec2670563b0b45f2643a0a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=-x\\,\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398549 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398549 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398549 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398549 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398549 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398549 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398549 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398549 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186398553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398549 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0c536b1b-39ee-59d3-8fef-dfde6d2dc504" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398550 #edb/ref 1080 "{y}^{2}\\ge -x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398550 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398550 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "158838e0-efdb-532f-9f9b-a61b3d97ab19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398551 #edb/ref 1080 "{y}^{2}\\le -x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398551 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398551 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ff58ee15-73c1-5580-9e71-8bba76a9b817" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398552 #edb/ref 1080 "{y}^{2}<-x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398552 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398552 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7091d7cf-fb36-5a53-885a-a308985da886" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398553 #edb/ref 1080 "{y}^{2}=-x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398553 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/r